  <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
  <p>Last updated: November 14, 2026.</p>
  <p>These terms are an agreement between you and Vestris Inc., the operator of this Posebook service. In these terms, "we" and "us" refer to Vestris Inc. By using the service, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use it. Questions about these terms can be sent to <%= mail_to "drawing@dblock.org" %>.</p>

  <h2>The Service</h2>
  <p>Posebook provides tools for recurring programs, invitations, participant profiles, and bookings. Program organizers remain responsible for their programs, venues, participation requirements, communications, and any arrangements made with participants. A booking in Posebook is a scheduling record, not a guarantee that a program will take place or that any separate payment or participation obligation has been fulfilled.</p>
  <p>You must have the legal capacity and any permissions required to use the service and participate in a program. If you act for an organization or another person, you must have authority to do so.</p>

  <h2>Accounts and Invitations</h2>
  <p>Provide accurate information, keep your password and private invitation links secure, and use only accounts and program access you are authorized to use. You are responsible for activity under your account and should report suspected unauthorized access promptly.</p>
  <p>Invitations, program permissions, and public-sharing preferences do not grant access to unrelated accounts or programs. Administrators and organizers may grant, pause, or revoke access within their authority.</p>

  <h2>Bookings and Program Arrangements</h2>
  <p>Review booking dates, times, time zones, venue information, and program instructions before confirming. Use the available cancellation and rescheduling features when plans change, and communicate directly with the organizer when needed. Calendar delivery and email invitations can be delayed, filtered, or unavailable; do not rely on them as the only record of an arrangement.</p>
  <p>Resolve questions about participation, compensation, venue conditions, cancellations, or disputes directly with the relevant organizer or participant. Posebook does not process payments or provide insurance or professional advice.</p>

  <h2>Your Content and Other People's Information</h2>
  <p>You retain rights to content you submit. You grant the service permission to store, process, and display that content as necessary to operate the features you use and according to the available visibility settings. You must have the rights and permissions needed to upload photos, provide personal information, and share content.</p>
  <p>Organizers must use participant information only for authorized program administration and related communications, respect sharing preferences, and protect private details and calendar access. Do not publish private participant information or forward private invitations without permission.</p>

  <h2>Acceptable Use</h2>
  <p>Do not use Posebook for unlawful activity, harassment, deception, unauthorized disclosure, or infringement of another person's rights. Do not attempt to bypass access controls, interfere with the service, distribute malicious software, or access or collect information you are not authorized to receive.</p>
  <p>We may restrict or suspend access to protect the service, address violations, comply with law, or respond to legitimate security concerns. Where appropriate, contact us to discuss a restriction or request assistance.</p>

  <h2>Privacy and Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>The <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path %> describes the service's data handling. Optional Google Calendar integration sends private booking details and invitations to Google and the authorized recipients. Organizers must choose a properly restricted calendar. Disconnecting does not remove events already created.</p>
  <p>Google, email providers, hosting providers, and other third-party services have their own terms and policies. Their availability and delivery behavior are outside Posebook's control.</p>

